.TH CBMAP_CONSTRUCT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cbmap_construct \- type-safe BST map construction
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cbstmap.h>

cbmap_construct(hm_name, key_type, val_type);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-safe macro for creating a BST map with default settings.
Automatically determines if keys are signed integers and creates type
marker variables for compile-time type checking.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name   Name of the BST map variable to create
key_type  Type of keys
val_type  Type of values
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Terminates program on allocation failure
Creates hidden type marker variables for type safety
Automatically determines key signedness and string key type
Uses default memory management and comparison
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cbmap_construct(map, int, char*);
cbmap_insert(map, 42, "hello");
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_construct_full (3),
.BR cbmap_create (3)
